The attached image (Figure 2) demonstrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are retained at the injection site and are gradually cleared over time in vivo. Whole-animal fluorescence imaging (Panel a) shows that the fluorescent signal from Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 persists at the injection sites for up to Day 21, with gradual reduction. Examination of excised organs (Panel b) on Day 21 reveals residual fluorescence primarily at the injection sites and draining lymph nodes, confirming localized retention without systemic accumulation. Quantitatively, Panel c shows the injection site's fluorescence intensity decreases significantly after Day 2 (p < 0.001), indicating a transient presence and clearance. This supports Nano-11's role as a localized adjuvant with minimal systemic distribution.